# juan_repro.dag — chain pengy's juan_reproduction end to end, unattended:
#   train (1 job) → apply (97-job array, one per run) → combine + evaluate.
#
# Submit from isolation_forest/:
#   mkdir -p logs condor/logs
#   condor_submit_dag condor/juan_repro.dag
#
# Node semantics: the apply node fails if ANY of its 97 procs exits non-zero
# (pengy's per-run script hard-fails on validation errors, e.g. a manifest
# path missing from EOS). RETRY re-runs the node — safe, since per-run
# publishes are atomic and idempotent. If a run fails persistently, DAGMan
# writes a rescue file; inspect the failing proc's .err under condor/logs/,
# then resubmit this DAG to resume from the rescue point.
JOB   train    condor/submit_train_juan_reproduction_digi_z8_if0001_train20_seed42.sub
JOB   apply    condor/submit_apply_juan_reproduction_digi_z8_if0001_train20_seed42_one_run.sub
JOB   combine  condor/submit_combineEval_juan_reproduction.sub

PARENT train  CHILD apply
PARENT apply  CHILD combine

RETRY train   1
RETRY apply   2
